<section class="hero">
  <h1>Brand</h1>
  <p>A cube over three ripples: the thing, and the echo of it.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>The mark</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Strokes only, on an <code>80&times;80</code> viewBox, colored by
    <code>currentColor</code> — so one file is legible on either theme.
  </p>

  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ '/brand/mark.svg' | url }}">mark.svg</a></h3>
        <p>Inline in a page header. Inherits <code>currentColor</code>.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ '/brand/logo.svg' | url }}">logo.svg</a></h3>
        <p>Standalone: README, og image, anywhere it is <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>-ed and has no text color to inherit.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ '/brand/favicon.svg' | url }}">favicon.svg</a></h3>
        <p>Tab icon. Heavier strokes and more spread, because at 16px the thin version fills in.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>Rules, such as they are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Don't re-tint it.</strong> It is <code>currentColor</code> on purpose; a brand-blue variant for dark headers is one more thing to keep in step.</li>
      <li><strong>Don't set it below 24px</strong> except as a favicon — the ripples merge.</li>
      <li><strong>Don't pair it with a second mark.</strong> A project's identity is its name in mono next to this one. The emoji-per-project habit is what this repo exists to end.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Color</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    <a href="https://github.com/cubicecho/cubeui" rel="noopener">cubeui</a>'s palette,
    under its names: a token says what the color means. Defined in
    <a href="{{ '/theme/cubesite.css' | url }}">cubesite.css</a>, and on their own in
    <a href="{{ '/brand/tokens.css' | url }}">tokens.css</a> for pages that want the
    palette without the stylesheet. Muted text and borders are not tokens — they
    are <code>--foreground</code> at 60% and 10%.
  </p>

  <ul class="swatches">
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--background)"></div><div class="label">--background</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--foreground)"></div><div class="label">--foreground</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--secondary)"></div><div class="label">--secondary</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--neutral)"></div><div class="label">--neutral</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--hover)"></div><div class="label">--hover</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--active)"></div><div class="label">--active</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--info)"></div><div class="label">--info</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--positive)"></div><div class="label">--positive</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--warning)"></div><div class="label">--warning</div></li>
    <li class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background: var(--negative)"></div><div class="label">--negative</div></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Type &amp; voice</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      System sans for prose. <strong>Mono for names</strong> — project titles,
      card headings, the wordmark on a project site — because every one of these
      names is also something you type. That contrast is most of the identity;
      keep it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Names are lowercase, as published: <code>mcp-router</code>, not "MCP
      Router". Taglines say what the thing <em>is</em>, in plain words, with no
      "blazing-fast", no "seamless", and no leading "A powerful".
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="readme-link">
    The long version lives in the repo:
    <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/brand/README.md" rel="noopener">brand/README.md</a>
  </p>
</section>
